### 2.1 Data Flow Summary

1. A commit lands on GitHub → webhook fires → ingestion pipeline pulls the diff.
1. Changed files are re-parsed; symbols, docstrings, and call edges are extracted.
1. Index stores are updated atomically (symbol table, vector index, call graph, manifest).
1. The MCP server serves queries against these stores via standardized tool calls.
1. The orchestrator runs an agent loop where the LLM calls MCP tools, drafts a test, and submits it to the validator.
1. The validator confirms every call exists in the manifest; on failure, the orchestrator hands the error back to the LLM for repair.

