## 4. Layer 2 — Index

### 4.1 Symbol Table (Postgres)

**Schema:**

```sql
CREATE TABLE symbols (
    id              TEXT PRIMARY KEY,            -- stable sha1 ID
    repo_id         TEXT NOT NULL,
    branch          TEXT NOT NULL,
    file_path       TEXT NOT NULL,
    qualified_name  TEXT NOT NULL,
    short_name      TEXT NOT NULL,
    kind            TEXT NOT NULL,                -- function|method|class|constant
    language        TEXT NOT NULL,
    signature       TEXT,                          -- raw signature string
    parameters      JSONB,                         -- [{name, type, default, kind}]
    return_type     TEXT,
    decorators      TEXT[],
    visibility      TEXT NOT NULL,                 -- public|private
    public_api      BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT false,
    docstring       TEXT,
    start_line      INT NOT NULL,
    end_line        INT NOT NULL,
    source_hash     TEXT NOT NULL,                 -- sha1 of body, for change detection
    stale           BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT false,
    updated_at      TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now()
);

CREATE INDEX idx_symbols_short_name        ON symbols (short_name);
CREATE INDEX idx_symbols_qualified_name    ON symbols (qualified_name);
CREATE INDEX idx_symbols_file              ON symbols (repo_id, branch, file_path);
CREATE INDEX idx_symbols_public_api        ON symbols (public_api) WHERE public_api;
CREATE INDEX idx_symbols_trgm_short_name   ON symbols USING gin (short_name gin_trgm_ops);
```

**Notes:**

- The trigram index supports fuzzy lookups (`find_symbol("conect_dvice")` still finds `connect_device`).
- `parameters JSONB` enables structural matching in `validate_call` without re-parsing the signature string.
- Always filter by `repo_id` and `branch`; never query globally.

### 4.2 Vector Index

**Choice:** `pgvector` if you already run Postgres (one less system); Qdrant or LanceDB if you need higher QPS or filtered ANN at scale.

**Chunking strategy:**

- One vector per **symbol**, not per file or per fixed-size window. Symbol-granular retrieval matches how the LLM reasons.
- Embed text composed as:
  
  ```
  <qualified_name>
  <signature>
  <docstring>
  <first N=40 lines of body>
  ```
- Truncate to embedding model’s max tokens; never split a symbol across vectors.

**Embedding model:**

- **Code-specialized** (preferred): a model trained on code such as a 768d or 1024d code embedding model. Generic text embeddings work but lose ~10-20% recall on identifier-heavy queries.
- Store the model name + version with the vector row so you can detect when an index needs a full rebuild.

**Schema (pgvector):**

```sql
CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS vector;

CREATE TABLE symbol_embeddings (
    symbol_id    TEXT PRIMARY KEY REFERENCES symbols(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    embedding    vector(768) NOT NULL,
    model        TEXT NOT NULL,
    model_ver    TEXT NOT NULL,
    embedded_at  TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now()
);

CREATE INDEX idx_symbol_embeddings_hnsw
    ON symbol_embeddings USING hnsw (embedding vector_cosine_ops)
    WITH (m = 16, ef_construction = 64);
```

**Distance metric:** cosine. Normalize embeddings at write time.

**Filtered ANN:** at query time, push filters (e.g. `public_api=true`, `language='python'`) via a join with `symbols` rather than into pgvector’s filter clause to keep the recall curve healthy.

### 4.3 Call Graph Storage

```sql
CREATE TABLE call_edges (
    caller_id      TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES symbols(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    callee_id      TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES symbols(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    call_site_line INT NOT NULL,
    confidence     TEXT NOT NULL,                  -- high|medium|low
    PRIMARY KEY (caller_id, callee_id, call_site_line)
);

CREATE INDEX idx_call_edges_callee ON call_edges (callee_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_call_edges_caller ON call_edges (caller_id);
```

For unresolved callees (dynamic dispatch), insert with `callee_id = NULL` and a `callee_hint` column for the best-effort name string. This still helps `find_usages` via name matching.

### 4.4 API Manifest

Materialized view rebuilt on every index update:

```sql
CREATE MATERIALIZED VIEW api_manifest AS
SELECT id, qualified_name, signature, parameters, return_type, docstring, file_path, start_line
FROM symbols
WHERE public_api = true AND NOT stale;
```

Served as a single JSON blob via the MCP resource `api://manifest`. Refresh after every batch ingest.

### 4.5 Test-to-Symbol Index

```sql
CREATE TABLE test_symbol_usage (
    test_id      TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES symbols(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    target_id    TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES symbols(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    PRIMARY KEY (test_id, target_id)
);

CREATE INDEX idx_test_symbol_usage_target ON test_symbol_usage (target_id);
```

Built by intersecting the call graph with the set of identified test functions. Powers `find_tests(symbol)`.

