## 10. Testing the MCP Server Itself

### 10.1 Unit Tests

- Per-tool tests with mocked storage.
- Schema conformance: every tool’s output validated against its declared JSON Schema.

### 10.2 Integration Tests

- A small fixture repo (~50 files, several known APIs, several known tests) checked into the project. Spin up Postgres + vector index in Docker, ingest the fixture, run a battery of queries with golden outputs.

### 10.3 Hallucination Regression Suite

- A list of known-bad function names (`conect_devicee`, `setupp`, etc.). Every release must return `exists=false` with sensible candidates.

### 10.4 End-to-End Generation Tests

- 20 representative test-generation scenarios. For each, run the full agentic loop; assert the validator passes and the generated test imports run (compile/parse only, not device-execute).

### 10.5 Performance Tests

- p50/p95/p99 per tool at target QPS.
- Cold-cache and warm-cache numbers reported separately.

